Subject: [PATCH] build: recognise rhel-* as a native Linux architecture

ecmc decides how to find the EtherCAT user library with:

    ifneq ($(filter linux-%,$(T_A)),)

which assumes every native Linux build uses the stock EPICS host
architecture name `linux-x86_64`.  EPICS has never required that, and sites
routinely define their own.  SLAC PCDS builds as `rhel9-x86_64`.

When the filter misses, the build silently takes the `else` branch -- the
Yocto cross-compile path -- where `$(SDKTARGETSYSROOT)` is unset:

    /usr/bin/ld: cannot find -lethercat

with the flags

    -L /usr/lib/etherlab -lethercat -Wl,-rpath=/usr/lib/etherlab

The space after `-L` is the tell: the native branch writes `-L$(ETHERLAB)/lib`
with no space, so that literal can only have come from line 38.  The failure
looks like a missing library and is actually a missed architecture test.
Nothing warns, because a cross-compile with no sysroot is indistinguishable
from a correctly configured one until the linker runs.

Note the value of `ETHERLAB` is irrelevant to this failure: the `else` branch
never references it.  It can be perfectly correct and you still get
`-L /usr/lib/etherlab`.

`rhel%` deliberately has no dash, unlike `linux-%` -- the arch name is
`rhel9-x86_64`, so `%` must absorb `9-x86_64`.  `rhel-%` would not match.

The block is duplicated verbatim in the example IOC, so both need it or the
example fails identically once the module itself builds.

Applies to: ecmc v11.0.8
Verified on: Rocky 9.8, EPICS_HOST_ARCH=rhel9-x86_64, EPICS base R7.0.3.1-2.0
---
 devEcmcSup/Makefile                   | 2 +-
 ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/devEcmcSup/Makefile b/devEcmcSup/Makefile
--- a/devEcmcSup/Makefile
+++ b/devEcmcSup/Makefile
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 USR_LDFLAGS += -lstdc++
 USR_CXXFLAGS += -std=c++17

-ifneq ($(filter linux-%,$(T_A)),)
+ifneq ($(filter linux-% rhel%,$(T_A)),)
 ETHERLAB ?= /opt/etherlab
 USR_INCLUDES += -I$(ETHERLAB)/include
 USR_CFLAGS += -fPIC
diff --git a/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile b/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
--- a/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
+++ b/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 USR_LDFLAGS_Linux += -Wl,--no-as-needed
 USR_CXXFLAGS += -std=c++17

-ifneq ($(filter linux-%,$(T_A)),)
+ifneq ($(filter linux-% rhel%,$(T_A)),)
 ETHERLAB ?= /opt/etherlab
 USR_INCLUDES += -I$(ETHERLAB)/include
 USR_CFLAGS += -fPIC
